{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197312",
      "title": "A Glance Under The Hood Of React Native",
      "lectureOrder": 4,
      "videoOrder": 3,
      "sourceHash": "f08a933ea60a7cd3785091bc2576edef3c4ccef5b2d3d8d943df1aa23adb3049",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.17,
          "end": 4.48,
          "en": "Now, how does React Native work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.48,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "Under The Hood though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.33,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "If you're building a React and React Native app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.86,
          "en": "then you are typically writing code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.86,
          "end": 15.56,
          "en": "which should look very familiar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.56,
          "end": 18.52,
          "en": "if you worked with React.js before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.52,
          "end": 20.79,
          "en": "maybe, or most likely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.79,
          "end": 23.71,
          "en": "for building browser based apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.71,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "This is a React Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 26.86,
          "en": "what you see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.86,
          "end": 28.11,
          "en": "And it's just one way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.11,
          "end": 29.84,
          "en": "of writing such a Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.84,
          "end": 32.84,
          "en": "We could also use the function keyword instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.84,
          "end": 34.87,
          "en": "of defining an arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.87,
          "end": 37.683,
          "en": "And we could also use a class based Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.56,
          "end": 39.84,
          "en": "But it's code like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.84,
          "end": 40.84,
          "en": "which you will write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 40.84,
          "end": 42.04,
          "en": "for React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 42.04,
          "end": 43.163,
          "en": "and it's code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 43.163,
          "end": 46.93,
          "en": "that will be compiled to Real Native App code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 46.93,
          "end": 48.58,
          "en": "So which will be bundled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 48.58,
          "end": 51.033,
          "en": "into a Real Native App in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 52.05,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "Now, if you take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 56.53,
          "en": "at the code snippet on the left here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 56.53,
          "end": 59.24,
          "en": "you will see two Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 59.24,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "two JSX elements in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 63.31,
          "en": "which you don't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 63.31,
          "end": 64.96,
          "en": "from web development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 64.96,
          "end": 68.27,
          "en": "the View and the Text element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 68.27,
          "end": 71.57,
          "en": "These are some of these special Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 71.57,
          "end": 74.09,
          "en": "that are exposed by React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 74.09,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "which will be compiled by React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 79.41,
          "en": "It is worth noting though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 81.6,
          "en": "that it's really just the Views.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 83.58,
          "en": "Just this JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 83.58,
          "end": 84.87,
          "en": "that is compiled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 84.87,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "not the JavaScript logic itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 89.743,
          "en": "I will come back to that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 91.94,
          "en": "So the Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 91.94,
          "end": 94.96000000000001,
          "en": "the JSX elements you use are compiled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 94.96000000000001,
          "end": 98.92,
          "en": "to native elements for the respective platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 98.92,
          "end": 101.25999999999999,
          "en": "And to make this a bit easier to understand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 101.25999999999999,
          "end": 104.09,
          "en": "take a look at this comparison table here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 104.09,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "here we got a bunch of elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 109.13,
          "en": "as we would use them in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 109.13,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "if we would be using react-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 113.4,
          "en": "and then the equivalence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 113.4,
          "end": 115.07,
          "en": "for the native platforms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 115.07,
          "end": 117.03999999999999,
          "en": "and then the Components exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 117.03999999999999,
          "end": 120.243,
          "en": "by React Native to target those equivalence.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 121.14,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "So for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 125.28,
          "en": "if you want to display an input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 125.28,
          "end": 128.33,
          "en": "where users can enter some text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 128.33,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "then when building a web app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 133.18,
          "en": "we would use the HTML input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 133.18,
          "end": 135.46,
          "en": "which is available in JSX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 135.46,
          "end": 137.633,
          "en": "when we're using react-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 138.69,
          "end": 141.73,
          "en": "If we would be building a native Android app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 141.73,
          "end": 144.01,
          "en": "with Java or Kotlin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 144.01,
          "end": 147.57999999999998,
          "en": "then it would be the built in added text widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 147.57999999999998,
          "end": 149.61,
          "en": "that is provided by Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 149.61,
          "end": 151.57999999999998,
          "en": "which we need to build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 151.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.413,
          "en": "For iOS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 152.413,
          "end": 154.82,
          "en": "it would be the UITextField element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 155.66,
          "end": 157.41,
          "en": "and with React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 157.41,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "we would use the built in TextInput Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 163.108,
          "en": "which is provided by React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 163.108,
          "end": 166.76,
          "en": "and which will then be compiled to added text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 166.76,
          "end": 171.013,
          "en": "for Android or to UITextField for iOS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 171.89,
          "end": 176.19,
          "en": "So React Native maps and compiles reusable Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 176.19,
          "end": 178.21,
          "en": "like TextInput or View",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 178.21,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "or many other Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 182.36,
          "en": "about which you will learn throughout the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 182.36,
          "end": 185.59,
          "en": "to their respective platform equivalents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 185.59,
          "end": 187.31,
          "en": "That's one of the main jobs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 187.31,
          "end": 189.053,
          "en": "React Native will take care of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 190.39,
          "end": 192.41,
          "en": "But what about the logic?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 192.41,
          "end": 194.51,
          "en": "I mentioned that those Views",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 194.51,
          "end": 197.8,
          "en": "the JSX elements are compiled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 197.8,
          "end": 200.3,
          "en": "to their native equivalence.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 200.3,
          "end": 202.15,
          "en": "But what about the JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 202.15,
          "end": 204.81,
          "en": "you write outside of JSX?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 204.81,
          "end": 206.57,
          "en": "What about all these functions?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 206.57,
          "end": 207.71,
          "en": "If statements?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 207.71,
          "end": 209.06,
          "en": "State management?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 209.06,
          "end": 210.153,
          "en": "What about that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 211.36,
          "end": 213.52,
          "en": "Well, unlike the UI elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 213.52,
          "end": 216.12,
          "en": "the logic is not compiled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 216.12,
          "end": 217.29,
          "en": "The UI elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 217.29,
          "end": 218.5,
          "en": "which are those Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 218.5,
          "end": 219.67000000000002,
          "en": "exposed by React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 219.67000000000002,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "are compiled as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 223.28,
          "en": "but the logic which you write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 223.28,
          "end": 226.16,
          "en": "in JavaScript is actually not compiled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 226.16,
          "end": 229.77,
          "en": "but instead it's running on a JavaScript thread",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 229.77,
          "end": 231.802,
          "en": "that's hosted by React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 231.802,
          "end": 235.09,
          "en": "in the native app that was built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 235.09,
          "end": 237.32999999999998,
          "en": "So React Native basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 237.32999999999998,
          "end": 241.31,
          "en": "spins up a simple JavaScript process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 241.31,
          "end": 243.56,
          "en": "as part of your native app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 243.56,
          "end": 244.44,
          "en": "that's being built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 244.44,
          "end": 247.27,
          "en": "And it manages this process for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 247.27,
          "end": 249.81,
          "en": "And it allows this process to talk",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 249.81,
          "end": 252.72,
          "en": "to the underlying native platform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 252.72,
          "end": 254.85,
          "en": "and therefore your JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 254.85,
          "end": 257.05,
          "en": "will run as JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 257.05,
          "end": 259.46,
          "en": "in the native app that's being built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 259.46,
          "end": 262.89,
          "en": "but it will then talk to the underlying Android",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 264.74,
          "en": "or iOS platform,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 264.74,
          "end": 267.98,
          "en": "through a basic translation bridge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 267.98,
          "end": 270.21,
          "en": "You could say that is provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 270.21,
          "end": 271.65,
          "en": "by React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 271.65,
          "end": 274.24,
          "en": "as part of your native app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 274.24,
          "end": 276.383,
          "en": "That's how you can think about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 277.32,
          "end": 279.47,
          "en": "And that is it for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 279.47,
          "end": 281.89,
          "en": "That's how React Native works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 281.89,
          "end": 284.57,
          "en": "Under The Hood and what it does for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 284.57,
          "end": 286.37,
          "en": "You don't need to know more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 286.37,
          "end": 287.73,
          "en": "You can of course dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 287.73,
          "end": 288.81,
          "en": "into the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 288.81,
          "end": 290.63,
          "en": "if you do want to learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 290.63,
          "end": 292.38,
          "en": "but that is what you should know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 292.38,
          "end": 294.92,
          "en": "in order to work with React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 294.92,
          "end": 297.315,
          "en": "because I believe it's always important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 297.315,
          "end": 301.29,
          "en": "to have a basic understanding of how a tool works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 301.29,
          "end": 303.793,
          "en": "And this is how React Native works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
